From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:44:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 66/75] wasm32: register variables also in procedures that use
 exceptions

tabstractvarsym.is_regvar excludes every procedure with
pi_uses_exceptions from register variables. That rule is for
setjmp/longjmp based exception handling, where the registers are not
valid anymore after the longjmp to the handler. On wasm32, exceptions
are branches within the same function (bf: a flag test after each call)
or wasm exception handling (try_table/catch, legacy try/catch), whose
handlers are blocks of the same function: wasm locals keep their values
there, and try/finally and try/except code is generated inline (no
outlined funclets that access the parent's frame). So allow register
variables in such procedures on wasm32.

Effect on the GocciaScript VM under wasmtime 49 (callgrind instruction
counts, AWFY geomean relative to native x86_64 -O4, research numbers):
1.95x -> 1.77x (most VM routines have try/finally blocks).
---
 compiler/symsym.pas | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/symsym.pas b/compiler/symsym.pas
index 61e89d9e..88b7c646 100644
--- a/compiler/symsym.pas
+++ b/compiler/symsym.pas
@@ -2005,7 +2005,11 @@ implementation
            - the value needs to be in memory (i.e. reference counted) }
         result:=(cs_opt_regvar in current_settings.optimizerswitches) and
                 not(pi_has_assembler_block in current_procinfo.flags) and
+{$ifndef wasm32}
+                { wasm: exceptions are branches (bf) or wasm EH within the same
+                  frame, wasm locals keep their values in the handlers }
                 not(pi_uses_exceptions in current_procinfo.flags) and
+{$endif wasm32}
                 not(pi_has_interproclabel in current_procinfo.flags) and
                 ((refpara and
                   (varregable <> vr_none)) or
